      "writtenOn": "2021-07-29T20:21:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it does do chunked allocs (the chunk size is an implementation detail, but in lib++ it\u0027s the same order-of-magnitude as what we chose internally).\n\nIt doesn\u0027t pre-alloc the first chunk (so that\u0027s one extra heap alloc to get the first block). But I think that\u0027s okay - we\u0027re talking about a pretty large block, and a single allocation to get it. Again, from the performance numbers - I can\u0027t even measure that overhead.",
      "parentUuid": "f4fe87ec_a8418c25",
      "revId": "994b3f77c855b6174700e058eea8754c051cf451",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
